Q: How to handle extension version updates and &quot;What&#39;s New&quot; pages in WXT? A: <p>WXT bundles this into the extension’s background script (service worker or persistent background depending on browser). This is the only place guaranteed to run on install/update.</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>export default defineBackground(() =&gt; {
  chrome.runtime.onInstalled.addListener(async (details) =&gt; {
    if (details.reason === &quot;update&quot;) {
      // your update logic
    }
  });
});
</code></pre>
<p>And use storage.defineStorage to ensure it runs exactly once if you need to.</p>
<pre><code>import { storage } from &quot;wxt/storage&quot;;

const versionStore = storage.defineItem&lt;string&gt;(&quot;app-version&quot;);

export default defineBackground(() =&gt; {
  chrome.runtime.onInstalled.addListener(async (details) =&gt; {
    const currentVersion = chrome.runtime.getManifest().version;
    const previousVersion = await versionStore.getValue();

    if (details.reason === &quot;update&quot; &amp;&amp; previousVersion !== currentVersion) {
      // Run your migration / &quot;What's New&quot; logic
      console.log(&quot;Extension updated:&quot;, previousVersion, &quot;→&quot;, currentVersion);

      // Example: open changelog page
      chrome.tabs.create({ url: chrome.runtime.getURL(&quot;whats-new.html&quot;) });

      // Save new version
      await versionStore.setValue(currentVersion);
    }

    // First install
    if (details.reason === &quot;install&quot;) {
      await versionStore.setValue(currentVersion);
    }
  });
});
</code></pre>
